    "type_designations": ["ZK840"],
    "module_designation": null,
    "description": "The indicating device is designated the Avery Weigh-Tronix ZK840. The indicator is self-indicating, mains, DC or battery-powered, and is designed to be used as part of a Class III Non-Automatic Weighing Instrument. The load receptor(s) may be BSQ digital bases and/or conventional platforms fitted with load cells. Construction: plastic (ABS) enclosure, mountable to a BSQ base or desk/wall mounted using an optional bracket. ISTN LCD display capable of positive and negative images; 6 operational keys plus touchscreen soft keys. Devices include: single or multi-range operation (maximum of 3 partial ranges), semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking, semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing, pre-set tare, stability determination and indication, display check, printing, gravity compensation, real time clock, command via external device (PC), counting, accumulation, checkweighing, target weighing, percentage weighing, grading, pick lists, kitting, density formulation, % recipe, connection to additional load receptors with identification of active load receptor(s), PLUs, piece weight selection, and extended indicating. Software designated AWT30-500208 version 2.x.x.x (x.x.x = non-legally relevant software); calibration and legally relevant parameters protected via sealed jumper or password with incrementing counters."
  },
